  "identity": {
    "playing_style": "Bosz's PSV are a possession-dominant, high-pressing 4-3-3 side that controls games through short passing and positional play, with fluid movement in the final third; the 2025/26 champions scored 101 league goals (27-3-4, 84 points, 19 ahead of Feyenoord). The flip side was 45 goals conceded and a 28th-place UCL league-phase exit, so Bosz has publicly made defensive solidity the priority for 2026/27 while keeping the attacking identity; a back-three was tested in pre-season.",
    "principles": [
      "develop-and-sell to the elite: Saibari to Bayern for ~EUR 50m (club record) follows Tillman/Lang/Bakayoko sales",
      "reinvest selectively in Eredivisie-proven Dutch talent (Mijnans EUR 13m from AZ) and cheap experienced back-ups (Kovar, Drommel)",
      "promote from Jong PSV (Merien, Van den Berg) and keep a young core (Babadi, Abed, Bajraktarevic, Van Bommel)",
      "coach continuity: Bosz contracted to mid-2028; GM Marcel Brands to 2029",
      "three titles in four seasons; UCL participation is a structural revenue pillar"
    ],
    "club_character": "Foundation-owned, corporate-rooted club (founded by Philips) with a stable, low-drama boardroom culture and a loyal, family-oriented fanbase at the Philips Stadion; pressure is about titles and UCL knockout progress rather than survival. Dutch media scrutiny is intense but civil; the club's 2025/26 UCL failure (28th) was the main criticism of a title season.",
    "ownership": "PSV NV (since 1 July 1999); its shares are held by the Stichting PSV Voetbal (board chaired by Eric van Schagen) plus one special/priority share held by the members' association Eindhovense Voetbalvereniging PSV. Philips is main sponsor, not a shareholder. General director Marcel Brands (since 2022, contract to mid-2029).",
    "political_and_social_context": "Publicly documented: PSV is historically the Philips company club and retains Philips as main sponsor; foundation-board changes announced by the club. No institution-level controversies were found in this research.",
    "languages": [
      "nl",
      "en"
    ],
    "wage_structure": "unknown (hierarchical in practice - Perisic, Schouten, Veerman presumed at the top; not verified)",
    "transfer_policy": "Sell one star per summer to a top-five league at EUR 30-50m (Saibari 2026, Tillman/Lang 2025, Bakayoko), buy Eredivisie-proven Dutch players and Bundesliga back-ups at EUR 5-15m, promote Jong PSV graduates; targets are 20-25 with resale value.",
